   "source": [
    "- CalEnviroScreen uses `-999` and `-1998` as *sentinel values* meaning “missing” or “not applicable”.  \n",
    "- We create a boolean mask that keeps only rows where **all** entries do not include `-999` and `-1998`.  \n",
    "- The cleaned DataFrame is stored in `X`.  \n",
    "- We print the number of original vs. cleaned rows to see how many tracts were removed."
   ]
  },
